{
  "answer_text": "Clients should anticipate the Official MCP Registry or its UI being slow or unavailable (manifesting as a “Loading servers...” state or a “Retry” prompt), which indicates transient failures, timeouts, or partial/unavailable discovery data. Resilient strategies are to detect and surface these states to the user, implement retries with a backoff strategy and retry UI, and provide fallback or cached discovery data or operator-configured endpoints so the client can fail gracefully or operate in degraded/read-only mode.",
  "source_quote": "Loading servers...\n\nRetry"
}

{
  "answer_text": "Detect the removal quickly (via periodic refreshes, cache invalidation, or subscribing to denylist feeds/webhooks) and immediately stop using discovery-based access to the denylisted server. Revoke or rotate any credentials or API tokens tied to that server, block or quarantine its endpoints, surface alerts to operators and affected users, and run audits to determine whether prior interactions require remediation. Maintain logs/evidence for forensics and, where possible, automate remediation (denylist hooks) to accelerate blocking and credential revocation.",
  "source_quote": "Registry maintainers can then denylist these entries and retroactively remove them from public access."
}

{
  "answer_text": "Keeping the server role distinct from the client role enforces a clear trust and operational boundary: servers mediate access, normalization, auditing, and backend integration while clients focus on orchestration, UI and agent behavior. This separation enables least-privilege security, reuse (many clients per server), independent scaling and upgrades, and simpler reasoning about access control and tenant isolation. Collapsing them into a monolith increases coupling and blast radius, makes auditing, access control and versioning harder, complicates deployment and horizontal scaling, and forces mixed responsibilities that raise operational and upgrade complexity.",
  "source_quote": "Create MCP servers to expose your data and tools"
}
